From a9e4420a1cb0c9b9c67b63b1a1c6b70fa6eec6a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: davmels <davmelous@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 00:22:02 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 53/61] llm_judge environment: grade free-form answers with a
 judge pool in a native run

A native environment (env name llm_judge) that grades the claim frame, or its last \boxed{} content,
against the reference with the judge model env.judge_pool serves. Modes: verdict (one token, reward
P(Yes) or P(Yes) >= 0.5) and justify (NVIDIA Gym equivalence prompt, [[A=B]]/[[A!=B]]). The judge pool
now also starts in native runs, after the trainer and inference clusters, and publishes its URLs in
Ray internal KV so native environments find it by name (judge_pool_address).

